  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the pathogenesis of NCI-H2170 through a series of mechanistically linked targets. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets NCI-H2170. This indicates a potential pathway where doxorubicin indirectly influences NCI-H2170 through the action of this compound. The shared involvement of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid in targeting both NCI-H1304 and NCI-H2170 suggests a possible role in the regulation of NCI-H2170, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of this compound in the targeting of NCI-H2170 support a mechanistic link, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction between doxorubicin and NCI-H2170.",
